        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n        \"The courtiers\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by bleeding pores and fatal scarlet stains, which has decimated the countryside. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, castellated abbey, sealing all entrances with iron gates and furnaces to ensure total isolation. Inside, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven elaborately themed rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their color scheme, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all music and dance. As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself—shrouded in grave-cloths and drenched in blood—causing terror and paralysis among the guests; when Prospero confronts the intruder with a dagger, the figure moves unchallenged through all seven rooms until, in the black chamber, it turns and Prospero dies instantly, revealing the figure to be empty, and the plague claims every reveller as darkness and decay consume the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\",\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a self-indulgent and authoritarian figure who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the Red Death, hosting a lavish, decadent masquerade while ignoring the suffering outside. His actions demonstrate a profound disregard for human life and a deep-seated denial of mortality, culminating in his violent, futile pursuit of a masked intruder who embodies the plague he sought to evade, leading to his immediate death and the collapse of his illusion of control.\",\n          \"source_position\": 1894,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero retreats to a sealed abbey to escape the plague\",\n          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, castellated abbey, sealing all entrances with iron gates and furnaces to ensure total isolation.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish, decadent masked ball while the plague rages outside\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 1894\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He reacts with rage and threats when confronted by the Red Death figure\",\n          \"quote\": \"Insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 11148\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He pursues the intruder with a dagger, driven by rage and fear\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12389\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He dies instantly upon confronting the intruder in the black chamber\",\n          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 12980\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The intruder is revealed to be empty, symbolizing the inevitability of death\",\n          \"quote\": \"gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled...\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1, Position 13136\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 18,\n      \"first_position\": 631,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...izure, progress and termination of the disease, were the incidents of half an hour. But the Prince Prospero was happy and dauntless and sagacious. When his dominions were half depopulated, he summoned to his...\",\n        \"...sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence. It was a volup...\",\n        \"...ith all the features of the face, was besprinkled with the scarlet horror. When the eyes of Prince Prospero fell upon this spectral image (which with a slow and solemn movement, as if more fully to sustain i...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"hi